Deliverable 2: Step-by-Step Installation Instructions (Update)
Document File: LLM Chatbot Installation Guide (MacBook Pro)
Prerequisites: You must complete the initial installation from the previous request (NewsAPI key, Python environment).
Step 1: Install and Configure Ollama 🧠
Download & Install: Download the Ollama application from their official website (https://ollama.com/) and install it on your MacBook Pro.
Launch: Ensure the Ollama app is running (it typically appears as a small icon in your menu bar).
Download the Model: Open your Terminal and download the Llama 3 LLM. This is required for the local summarization:
Bash
ollama run llama3
# Wait for the download to complete, then type 'exit' to close the session.


Step 2: Update Project Files
Open your Terminal and navigate back to your project directory:
Bash
cd ai-news-chatbot


Update requirements.txt: Use your text editor (nano or VS Code) to replace the content of requirements.txt with the new, updated list (it now includes ollama).
Create/Replace news_chatbot_llm.py: Rename your old file and create the new one, pasting the updated Python code above into news_chatbot_llm.py. Remember to replace YOUR_NEWS_API_KEY with your actual key.
Step 3: Install New Dependency
Activate Virtual Environment:
Bash
source venv/bin/activate


Install the new ollama Python library:
Bash
pip install -r requirements.txt


Step 4: Run the LLM Chatbot! 🚀
Execute the new Python script:
Bash
python3 news_chatbot_llm.py


The chatbot will now fetch the articles, send the text to the local Llama 3 model (via Ollama) for summarization, and then display the concise summaries. Note: The first time you summarize, it may be slightly slower as the model loads.

Deliverable 3: Instructions for Uploading to GitHub (Update)
The process is the same, but we will commit and push the new files.
Step 1: Commit the Updated Files
Make sure you are in your project folder (ai-news-chatbot) and the virtual environment is deactivated (deactivate if needed).
Add the new and updated files to the staging area:
Bash
git add .


Commit the changes with a clear message:
Bash
git commit -m "Feature: Integrated local LLM (Ollama/Llama 3) for news summarization"


Step 2: Push to GitHub
Push the committed changes to your remote repository:
Bash
git push


Your GitHub repository will now contain the LLM-powered news chatbot code! This YouTube video provides a good overview of how to set up an LLM locally. How to Run Llama 3 Locally

